# Frontend (SPA) configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` for local overrides, or set these as BUILD-TIME
# environment variables on your static host (Render static site `transform-web`).
#
# Vite inlines `VITE_*` variables into the bundle at build time, so
# `VITE_API_BASE_URL` must be present when `npm run build` runs — setting it
# only at runtime has no effect.
#
# The React app is hosted separately from the API and talks to it cross-origin,
# so the API must allow this SPA's origin in `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` and in the
# object-storage bucket CORS list (`S3_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`).

# Base URL of the Transform API, including the `/api` prefix.
#
# Local development: the Vite dev server proxies `/api` -> http://localhost:8000
# (see vite.config.ts), so `/api` keeps requests same-origin. Keep this default.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Production (Render static site): point at the API origin, e.g.
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://transform-api-7b3g.onrender.com/api
